    "narrative": "The Ghost Ride the WHIP lineup is primed for a high-ceiling performance today, spearheaded by the elite speed-power combination of **Corbin Carroll** (81.14) and the favorable platoon profile of **Trevor Story** (75.93). **Corbin Carroll** is our strongest play, benefiting from a soft matchup against Pecko (xERA 6.19) and a significant +6% boost from his dynamic platoon advantage. Similarly, **Jose Caballero** (74.42) remains a critical anchor for our stolen base pursuit; despite hitting 8th, his +13% dynamic platoon edge against Ray makes him an essential start, even with the structural penalty of his batting order. We are also capitalizing on **Vinnie Pasquantino** (72.92) facing the deteriorating stuff of Scherzer; his +14% platoon efficiency represents one of our most significant situational edges of the slate.\n\nThe bench decision process was disciplined, with **Austin Riley** (43.98) narrowly missing the cut. While **Austin Riley** provides power, he was effectively neutralized by a difficult matchup against Wheeler (xERA 3.27), and the structural necessity of prioritizing our higher-floor starters forced him to the pine. We are monitoring **James Wood** (49.75) closely; his matchup against Glasnow is objectively dangerous given the pitcher\u2019s elite strikeout profile (xERA 2.91), yet his position at the top of the lineup and an elite 0.418 xwOBA keep him just inside our start threshold. We remain cautious regarding **Seiya Suzuki** (58.75) and **Cole Young** (48.61), both of whom are facing \"Elite Hold\" catchers\u2014the scouting data suggests a 60\u201362% success rate for SB attempts, which slightly dampens their overall efficiency scores. With **Giancarlo Stanton** confirmed on the IL, we are managing our remaining depth carefully to preserve games, keeping prospects like **Travis Bazzana**, **Edwin Arroyo**, and **Dalton Rushing** in reserve while **Tyler Soderstrom** and **Brice Turang** remain on the periphery of our daily utility calculations.",
